From 5384cb456f684bead2006fd2be38d21bfc7134db Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Romeo Mattar <romeomat.work@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 17:40:40 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] hw/misc: add sim-clock, virtual clock read-out and
 exact-time stop

QMP can pause a VM, but not at a given virtual time outside of
record/replay. A host that drives a simulation (feeding sensor data,
running a test for N ms of guest time) needs exactly that. sim-clock is
a bus-less device with a chardev: the host can read QEMU_CLOCK_VIRTUAL
and ask for the VM to be paused when it reaches a given time. Under
-icount the vCPUs get no budget past a pending virtual deadline, so the
stop lands on the same guest instruction on every run. Resuming is left
to QMP "cont".

Example:
  -chardev socket,id=clk,path=/tmp/clk.sock,server=on,wait=off
  -device sim-clock,chardev=clk

Signed-off-by: Romeo Mattar <romeomat.work@gmail.com>
---
 hw/misc/Kconfig     |   4 +
 hw/misc/meson.build |   1 +
 hw/misc/sim_clock.c | 187 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 192 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 hw/misc/sim_clock.c

